-      <guid>http://localhost:1314/blog/building-production-llm-systems/</guid>
+      <guid>https://danielfiuza.com/blog/building-production-llm-systems/</guid>
       <description>&lt;p&gt;Two years building production LLM systems taught me that &lt;strong&gt;research prototypes ≠ production systems&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-reality-check&#34;&gt;The Reality Check&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our customer vulnerability prediction system started with GPT-4 for everything. Great demos, terrible production:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Too slow (5+ seconds)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Too expensive (£100+ per 1000 requests)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Unreliable at scale&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-actually-works&#34;&gt;What Actually Works&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;1-hybrid-architecture&#34;&gt;1. Hybrid Architecture&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Input → Fast Classifier → [High Confidence] → Response&#xA;           ↓&#xA;      [Uncertain] → LLM → Human Review → Response&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result&lt;/strong&gt;: 80% handled by fast models, 10x cost reduction.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
     </item>
     <item>
       <title>Adding Images to Your Hugo Portfolio</title>
-      <link>http://localhost:1314/blog/adding-images-hugo/</link>
+      <link>https://danielfiuza.com/blog/adding-images-hugo/</link>
       <pubDate>Sun, 15 Dec 2024 10:00:00 +0600</pubDate>
-      <guid>http://localhost:1314/blog/adding-images-hugo/</guid>
+      <guid>https://danielfiuza.com/blog/adding-images-hugo/</guid>
       <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;adding-images-to-your-hugo-portfolio&#34;&gt;Adding Images to Your Hugo Portfolio&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Images make your portfolio and blog posts much more engaging and professional. Here&amp;rsquo;s how you can add them to both your blog posts and portfolio projects.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;blog-post-images&#34;&gt;Blog Post Images&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;method-1-featured-image-in-frontmatter&#34;&gt;Method 1: Featured Image in Frontmatter&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Add an &lt;code&gt;image&lt;/code&gt; field to your blog post&amp;rsquo;s frontmatter:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div style=&#34;color:#4d4d4d;background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table style=&#34;border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&#34;vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#4d4d4d;background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f&#34;&gt;1&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f&#34;&gt;2&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f&#34;&gt;3&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f&#34;&gt;4&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;&lt;td style=&#34;vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#4d4d4d;background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-yaml&#34; data-lang=&#34;yaml&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;---&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cbcbcb&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cbcbcb&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#2c5dcd;font-weight:bold&#34;&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cbcbcb&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#0c6&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Your Blog Post Title&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cbcbcb&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cbcbcb&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#2c5dcd;font-weight:bold&#34;&gt;image&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cbcbcb&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#0c6&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;/images/blog/your-image.jpg&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cbcbcb&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cbcbcb&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;---&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cbcbcb&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;method-2-images-in-content&#34;&gt;Method 2: Images in Content&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You can also add images directly in your markdown content:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
     </item>
     <item>
       <title>Building Blockchain Security at Scale</title>
-      <link>http://localhost:1314/blog/first-blog/</link>
+      <link>https://danielfiuza.com/blog/first-blog/</link>
       <pubDate>Thu, 01 Aug 2024 12:14:34 +0600</pubDate>
-      <guid>http://localhost:1314/blog/first-blog/</guid>
+      <guid>https://danielfiuza.com/blog/first-blog/</guid>
       <description>&lt;p&gt;After years building AI systems for healthcare and LLMs, I&amp;rsquo;ve found my most challenging and impactful work yet: &lt;strong&gt;blockchain security and compliance at Range.org&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-transition-to-blockchain&#34;&gt;The Transition to Blockchain&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Moving from traditional ML to blockchain required learning entirely new paradigms:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Healthcare AI&lt;/strong&gt;: Structured data, regulated environments, batch processing&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Blockchain ML&lt;/strong&gt;: Graph data, pseudonymous actors, real-time requirements&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The shift wasn&amp;rsquo;t just technical—it was philosophical. In blockchain, &lt;strong&gt;trust is code&lt;/strong&gt;, and every system must be designed for adversarial environments.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
     </item>
     <item>
       <title>Hugo Portfolio Website</title>
-      <link>http://localhost:1314/portfolio/hugo-portfolio-website/</link>
+      <link>https://danielfiuza.com/portfolio/hugo-portfolio-website/</link>
       <pubDate>Fri, 19 Jun 2020 23:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
-      <guid>http://localhost:1314/portfolio/hugo-portfolio-website/</guid>
+      <guid>https://danielfiuza.com/portfolio/hugo-portfolio-website/</guid>
       <description>&lt;p&gt;I created my portfolio website using Hugo and UIKit, it serves as an online resume containing all my work.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This has been created as a theme so that others can use and adapt it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;sections&#34;&gt;Sections&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;homepage&#34;&gt;Homepage&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://res.cloudinary.com/samrobbins/image/upload/q_auto/v1591885280/screenshot_aexm2m.png&#34; alt=&#34;Homepage Screenshot&#34; title=&#34;Homepage Screenshot&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The homepage provides the basic information about you, including links to social media, skills you have, things you&amp;rsquo;ve done and your education. This page makes good use of UIKit grid and cards for organising all the information and ensuring it is responsive to work on mobile devices. The hackathon section of this page uses code from &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/web-tiki/responsive-grid-of-hexagons&#34; title=&#34;https://github.com/web-tiki/responsive-grid-of-hexagons&#34;&gt;https://github.com/web-tiki/responsive-grid-of-hexagons&lt;/a&gt; to ensure that the hexagons tile correctly.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
     </item>
     <item>
       <title>About</title>
-      <link>http://localhost:1314/about/_index_new/</link>
+      <link>https://danielfiuza.com/about/_index_new/</link>
       <pubDate>Sun, 12 May 2019 12:14:34 +0600</pubDate>
-      <guid>http://localhost:1314/about/_index_new/</guid>
+      <guid>https://danielfiuza.com/about/_index_new/</guid>
       <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;daniel-fiuza&#34;&gt;Daniel Fiuza&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Data Scientist&lt;/strong&gt; at Range.org with a &lt;strong&gt;PhD from Imperial College London&lt;/strong&gt;. I build ML systems for blockchain security and compliance—protecting $30B+ in monitored assets across 21 integrated chains.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;what-i-do&#34;&gt;What I Do&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;🔗 &lt;strong&gt;Blockchain ML&lt;/strong&gt;: Anomaly detection and risk analytics for DeFi protocols and cross-chain bridges&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;💰 &lt;strong&gt;Stablecoin Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;: USDC monitoring via CCTP, KYT/AML systems, and transaction risk scoring&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;🛡️ &lt;strong&gt;Security Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;: Real-time threat detection and incident response for blockchain networks&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;🔬 &lt;strong&gt;Research&lt;/strong&gt;: ML for biomarker discovery at Imperial College London (part-time)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;current-focus&#34;&gt;Current Focus&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Data Scientist at Range.org&lt;/strong&gt; — building the blockchain security and intelligence platform trusted by leading protocols. Our ML-powered suite monitors $30B+ in assets, processes 730M+ transactions, and provides real-time compliance solutions for stablecoins and DeFi.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
     </item>
